@startuml
title Service Consumption using NaaS and E2E Service Management

participant "Fixed Access Domain\nServiceCatalogManagement" as FA
participant "Copper Domain\nServiceCatalogManagement" as CO
participant "Soft Service Domain\nServiceCatalogManagement" as SS
participant "Network Service Domain\nServiceCatalogManagement" as NS
participant "Centralised\nServiceCatalogManagement" as CSM
participant "EventBus" as Bus #grey
participant "E2E SM Domain\nServiceCatalogManagement" as E2E
participant "Product Catalog Management" as PCM

FA -> CSM : 1 **POST Service Specification TMF633**\n**Fiber Fixed Access**
CSM -> Bus : 2 Service Specification Create Event
Bus -> E2E : 3 Service Specification Create Listener

CO -> CSM : 4 **POST Service Specification TMF633**\n**Copper Access**
CSM -> Bus : 5 Service Specification Create Event
Bus -> E2E : 6 Service Specification Create Listener

NS -> CSM : 7 **POST Service Specification TMF633**\n**Fix Connectivity**
CSM -> Bus : 8 Service Specification Create Event
Bus -> E2E : 9 Service Specification Create Listener

E2E -> E2E : 10 Perform Composite Service Design

E2E -> CSM : 11 **POST Service Specification TMF633**\n**E2E Connectivity Service**
CSM -> Bus : 12 Service Specification Create Event
Bus -> PCM : 13 Service Specification Create Listener

SS -> CSM : 14 **POST Service Specification TMF633**\n**TV Service**
CSM -> Bus : 15 Service Specification Create Event
Bus -> PCM : 16 Service Specification Create Listener

note over CSM, E2E
  NOTE:
  1. Step 2, 5, 8 can also be listened by Product Catalog
  2. Step 1, 4, 7 - Alternatively the centralised catalog can
  perform GET based on an event published by the catalog of each domain
end note

@enduml
